{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nThe sine function has a period of $2\\pi .$ Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-16227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=n\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Assuming that $n$ is an integer, the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+bn,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+bn,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2}.$ Find the values of ${\\theta }_{1}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}$ in $[0,2\\pi ),$ and the value of $b.$\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $4$th quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/5af1febb2c8dbf1b19ee64addd8f8ccdd5a30f9330d36ab800475fce9f6740c2.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nWriting this as $x=\\theta +2n\\pi ,$ where $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ we get\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$ ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ and $b=2\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322283" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/c722d4fa2b77011e4df5b086c19bb09943446941484cfaf87559ca39a52183bc.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={315}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-120762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={240}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={300}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}?$  Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $4$th quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/b3c523e882baf0b3a105e10131091e40de686b4c1483f46e7bdc235e30743a6d.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nWriting this as $x={\\theta }^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},$ where $\\theta \\in [0,360),$ we get\n\n$$\nx={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-120767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={240}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] ["math" "x={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x={210}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={330}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the general solution to the equation  $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}?$  Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/bf1efb64724fb0dfbf60cc14905e63ba867caa0bf0edd888b35fb554af97c856.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-16228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-16228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-76736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the general solution to the equation $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2=0?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-76736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{-\\sqrt{2}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arcsin}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $4$th quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/87b3a90142f4c810433bd2c219382379fc508fa426567708abddb744f39771c2.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nWriting this as $x=\\theta +2n\\pi ,$ where $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ we get\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-76736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-76736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-76736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-76736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Assuming that $n$ is an integer, the general solution to the equation $3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-6=0$ is given by \n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+bn,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+bn,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2}.$ Find the values of ${\\theta }_{1}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}$ in $[0,{360}^{∘}),$ and the value of $b.$\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-6 & =0 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & =6 \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡x & =\\frac{6}{3\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arccos}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/cf16066cb8b8368129be39a22f5c15727ac698f44d6f870511c2e07ec317d643.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={315}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n,\\,x={315}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=45\\,{\\,}^{∘},$ ${\\theta }_{2}=315\\,{\\,}^{∘},$ and $b=360\\,{\\,}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "45"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "315"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-322656" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "360"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\sqrt{2}?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arccos}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/c722d4fa2b77011e4df5b086c19bb09943446941484cfaf87559ca39a52183bc.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $4$th quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={360}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={315}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "987f404ca61dd5e1564c1e3cf4654c143a9fdae95d95829181389d88f8fff849"} {"question" "q-120772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/state.json" "file_sha256" "38d9e5c26a5f674a27efbbd96ae3747c48b46eaa263ccb97fea15be94f29dd07"} {"question" "q-120772" "fie